 "notes": ["Quarters before Yahoo's 5-quarter window (the year-over-year base) and figures Yahoo's statements lack are from the company's DART filings (consolidated statements); a fiscal Q4 is the annual report minus the Q3 report's nine-month figures, diluted EPS included (computed ones are listed in \"derived\").", "PBR: book value per share uses the shares outstanding of all share classes (common + preferred, without treasury shares; DART), as Korean BPS does.", "Cash flow from the company's DART filings (영업활동 현금흐름; capex = 유형자산의 취득, purchases of property, plant and equipment): the reports' cash-flow statements are year-to-date, so Q2 = H1 - Q1, Q3 = 9M - H1 and Q4 = full year - 9M. FCF = operating cash flow - capex. FCF QoQ / YoY only between two positive values.", "Q1 25: computed as the fiscal year minus its other three quarters where Yahoo's quarterly statements lack them; the fields are listed in \"derived\".", "Q4 24, FY21: diluted EPS from Yahoo's reported EPS where it matches net income / diluted shares, else net income / diluted shares (Yahoo's statements lack it).", "Fiscal labels are the company's own fiscal year, named by the calendar year it ends in.", "PER uses the trailing 4 quarters' diluted EPS (annual: the year's), ROA the trailing 4 quarters' net income over average total assets. The (E) EPS is the analysts' consensus, on Yahoo's EPS basis (\"EPS (Yahoo basis)\": for US companies usually adjusted, non-GAAP)."]
